---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="John Morgan"
  description="Engineering leader and Fractional CTO. Experience, projects, and engineering philosophy."
>
  <SiteHeader active="home" />

  <main>
    <section id="intro">
      <p class="lead">
        I build and lead engineering teams. Most recently I was Head of Engineering at ManageXR,
        where the engineering org grew from 3 people to 15. Before that I spent four years on
        Google's Search Ranking team. I like shipping real products with small teams, and I treat
        security and compliance as a design constraint from day one.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        I also do Fractional CTO and engineering advisory work through <a
          href="https://faebriel.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Faebriel</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="philosophy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Philosophy</span>
      <h2>How I think about engineering</h2>
      <p>
        Good software should feel like magic to the user and boring to maintain. Most of the risk
        in a codebase comes from small decisions nobody owned or revisited. The hard problems you
        see coming tend to get handled. I lead from inside the code, because the fastest way to
        set a standard is to show it in a diff.
      </p>
      <p>
        I adopted AI-native engineering early and push for it, because teams that use it well
        ship faster without lowering their bar. At ManageXR I drove adoption across the company,
        from engineering workflows to customer support tooling.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/philosophy">Read the full philosophy &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="experience">
      <span class="eyebrow">Experience</span>
      <h2>Work &amp; education</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>ManageXR · Head of Engineering</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">Oct 2021 – May 2026</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Grew the engineering and QA team from 3 to 15. Owned architecture, hiring, and
          engineering standards, and stayed hands-on in backend and Android. Led
          security and compliance for the company (SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001) and worked with
          enterprise customers and partners during sales.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Google · Senior Software Engineer, Tech Lead</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">2017 – 2021</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Led technical direction for a critical Search Ranking backend component and reduced
          recall loss by more than 10% with large-scale ETL and feature engineering. Redesigned the
          deep neural network in the serving path, cutting tail latency by 15ms. Built the testing
          infrastructure for a major infrastructure redesign.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Stanford University · B.S. Computer Science</h3>
          <span class="entry-meta">Class of 2017</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Human-Computer Interaction track. 1st place, CS Department Software Fair, for disaster
          response software. Debate Society captain, 2014–2016.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="read-more"><a href="/experience">See full experience and projects &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="consulting">
      <span class="eyebrow">Consulting</span>
      <h2>Fractional CTO &amp; advisory</h2>
      <p>
        I take on a small number of Fractional CTO and advisory engagements with founder-led
        software companies: technical strategy, hands-on execution, security and enterprise
        readiness, and team building.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/consulting">See consulting services &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <div class="links-row">
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/jnmorgan5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/john-at-faebriel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="mailto:john5morgan29@gmail.com">Email</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter showHobbies />
</Layout>
